title: 'statement-store: keep a transient statement until its outboxes fetch it'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On nodes running the v2 DHT statement path, a transient statement stays in the store until
    every propagation outbox it was queued in has fetched it, instead of being swept as soon as the
    propagation pass takes it. `StatementStore` gains `hold_statements` and `release_statements`,
    both no-ops by default, and every statement `take_recent_statements` returns comes with one
    hold that the caller releases. The new `substrate_sub_statement_store_held_statements` gauge
    reports how many statements are held. Nodes without the v2 DHT path enabled are unaffected.

crates:
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
